# Line endings are LF in the working tree on EVERY platform.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows checks text files out as CRLF, and every test
# that compares a fixture's bytes to what the code produces fails on an
# invisible \r: three precomputed QR matrices and three theme files did, on the
# first Windows run that got far enough to compare anything. The code writes LF
# and the fixtures are recorded as LF, so the working tree should hold LF too.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Recorded bytes, not text — never touched, never normalised.
*.pptx binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.m4a binary
*.wav binary
*.woff2 binary

# Review comments are an APPEND-ONLY log (SPEC REVIEW), and this line is what
# makes that pay off: two reviewers commenting on the same deck at the same time
# produce two sets of added lines, and git takes both instead of asking somebody
# to resolve a conflict in a file nobody edits by hand.
#
# It works because nothing ever rewrites a line — resolving a comment and
# replying to one are records of their own. A store that mutated a line would
# conflict on exactly the deck that two people were reviewing.
*.review.jsonl merge=union
